## Project summary (elevator pitch)

Build an end-to-end differentiable cosmology pipeline that treats a cosmological forward model (initial density → evolved matter → mock observations) as a differentiable function, and uses gradient-based and learned inference to reconstruct posterior samples or MAP estimates of the initial conditions conditioned on observed structure. The aim is to demonstrate practical field-level inversion at progressively realistic scales and produce open, reproducible code + diagnostics.

Key novel value: combine modern autodiff stacks and ML samplers with scalable simulation and observation realism to make inverse cosmology practical and reusable.

