## Risks & mitigations

- **Memory blow-up when backpropagating through time loops**
    
    *Mitigation:* implement reversible symplectic integrators and/or adjoint recomputation checkpointing; use chunked time-stepping.
    
- **Model mismatch (bias due to simplistic observational model)**
    
    *Mitigation:* progressively add observational complexities; include flexible nuisance parameters and marginalize them.
    
- **Posterior sampling in very high dim is infeasible**
    
    *Mitigation:* focus on MAP & amortized inference; test MCMC on reduced-dim subspaces; evaluate Laplace approximations.
    
- **Baryons / subgrid physics break small-scale reconstructions**
    
    *Mitigation:* restrict target scales, use emulator or marginalized nuisance models for baryonic effects.
    

